In my recent flame mage ascension (see my other post), I noted that
Medusa behaves differently from the past. I arrived at her lair with an
amulet of reflection and a blindfold (which is my paranoid approach -- I
know that the amulet would be sufficient, but I blindfold myself
nonetheless). I expected that as usual she would die when I woke her up,
due to my amulet reflecting her gaze. She did not die, instead escaped
to the level below where I had to follow her using a blessed scroll of
teleportation. When I killed her finally, I experienced the birth of
Pegasus -- for the first time ever. I would have liked to tame him, to
avoid that my pet Archon killed him. Knowing he did not eat, I tried to
throw him a gem -- after all, he looks like a white unicorn. The gem
just hit him and made him angry... Too bad.

Later, I checked in wizard mode, how the game behavior has been changed
(from 0.0.7E6F3 to 0.7E7F3). I paid Medusa a visit with either an amulet
of reflection or a shield of reflection and no blindfold this time. Each
time her gaze was reflected, but "Medusa does not seem to notice her
gaze is reflected" (or a similar message), so she does not get stoned
anymore by these two items. A mirror, applied in her direction, still
works. Since Perseus killed her with his shield, this is an additional
separation from the myth.

I then decided to also try the action of reflection on the Beholder.
Interestingly, a silver scale mail seems to behave differently for him
than an amulet of reflection (I did not try the shield of reflection,
but guess it works as the amulet). The amulet reflects his gaze and
kills him. The mail does not (at least not immediately). He can still
cause pain to you with his gaze and stun you. (Was not killed despite
not having magic protection, but this may be an accident. Maybe the
Beholder typically needs some attempts, before his gaze actually kills you.)


